Omission
- [N1] Omitted trace (input 1): i1:Initially, the appointment approval form is sent. -> i2:After that, the approval is received. -> i3:Following the approval, there is a contact with TS to clarify the timing. -> i4:Once the approval is received, it is checked. -> i5:If the resource is internal, the appointment is authorized. -> i7:After the approval, the mandatory documentation along with the approval is sent to HR services. -> i8:The form is then scanned and recorded into the GovSource system. -> i9:The approval is checked and then sent along with the mandatory documentation to HR services. -> i12:However, if there are variations, a business case is completed. -> i10:HR services receive the documentations and this marks the end of the process.
- [N2] Omitted trace (input 2): i1:Initially, the appointment approval form is sent. -> i2:After that, the approval is received. -> i3:Following the approval, there is a contact with TS to clarify the timing. -> i4:Once the approval is received, it is checked. -> i5:If the resource is internal, the appointment is authorized. -> i7:After the approval, the mandatory documentation along with the approval is sent to HR services. -> i8:The form is then scanned and recorded into the GovSource system. -> i9:The approval is checked and then sent along with the mandatory documentation to HR services. -> i13:However, if there are variations, a business case is completed and attached. -> i10:HR services receive the documentations and this marks the end of the process.
